@startuml
' ── CURRENT STATE: PROVEO CHOOSES NO AGENT MODEL BY ENVIRONMENT ───────────
' Rehomed 2026-10-17 from _spec/_plans/retire-model-bridging.puml, which now
' holds only its two open questions, Q2 (local model) and Q4 (the catalog)
' (repo-simplification.puml N10). This block is the live design; the diagram
' below it is the RETIRED mechanism, kept for the one fact noted after it.
'
' THE DECISION (operator, 2026-09-09; not re-argued). An agent's model comes
' from ITS OWN SAVED CONFIG, carried between sessions by the durable home
' (_spec/packages/lib/config-seeding-and-persistence.puml). A first run gets
' the agent's own built-in default. proveo seeds no model id: seeding one
' would be proveo choosing again. Answers recorded with it: Q1 the agent's own
' default · Q3 roles survive as the CREDENTIAL vocabulary · Q5 no first-run
' announcement · Q6 the apply_model_bridges call sites were removed, not
' emptied, because a no-op left in place reads as a live mechanism.
'
' WHAT LANDED. Deleted: defs/bridges/ (four TSV tables + README),
' internal/provider/slots.go (BridgeTable, ResolvedEnv and kin),
' embed.ModelBridges, run.Spec.ModelBridges, Params.Bridges,
' sandbox.Input.Bridges / ResolvedModelEnv, posture.MergeRoles, the four
' `COPY defs/bridges/` layers, apply_model_bridges and its four call sites.
' Pruned from roles.go: RolesFrom (the env read), Canonical, ResolveRoles,
' PlanFallback. MEASURED 2026-10-17:
'   provider.RoleNames (roles.go:15; was RoleVars) names ARCHITECT_MODEL,
'     EDITOR_MODEL, SMALL_MODEL as the KEYS of a remembered assignment
'     (provider.Roles). The name drops "Vars" so nobody reads them from env.
'   posture.RolesLine (posture.go:223) renders roles directly; no slot table.
'   The credential and billing surface still reads roles: Roles.MissingKeys,
'     WithheldKeys, BillingClashes (roles.go:36-87), and the choice UI rows
'     (_spec/internal/choiceui/wireframe.puml). None of them sets a model.
'
' A HARNESS'S OWN MODEL VAR IS THE OPERATOR CONFIGURING THAT HARNESS.
' OPENCODE_MODEL, CURSOR_MODEL, CODEX_MODEL, ANTHROPIC_MODEL pass
' through untouched (CODING_HARNESSES.md "Models are not bridged"). A retirement that
' dropped them would have taken a working control with it. The host still
' warns on an unknown id in one of them: run.assembleEnv → warnUnknownModel
' (internal/run/helpers.go:66-74) → provider.CheckModel.
'
' A SEED NAMES NO MODEL. opencode substitutes an UNSET {env:VAR} with "", so
' the old seed's "model": "{env:OPENCODE_MODEL}" pinned the model to NOTHING
' in the durable home. MEASURED: defs/opencode/sample_opencode.json and
' defaults/opencode.json carry no model key and no {env:OPENCODE…};
' plan/build omit theirs and inherit the global.
'
' --local-model IS THE ONE CALLER THAT STILL SELECTS A MODEL, per harness,
' from PROVEO_LOCAL_MODEL and never from a role name. opencode needs its own
' block because the bridge alone used to name its local model:
' configure_opencode_local_model (defs/opencode/entrypoint.sh:25-70) registers
' the ollama provider AND sets .model and .agents.title.model. claudecode reads
' ANTHROPIC_MODEL from sbx.LocalModelEnv. Whether this carve-out is permanent
' is retire-model-bridging Q2.
'
' CREDENTIAL BRIDGES ARE A DIFFERENT MECHANISM WITH THE SAME NAME. The
' GEMINI_API_KEY → GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY alias maps a credential, not a
' model; deleting the model half took it along on the first attempt, and a
' parity test caught the loss. It survives (TestOneGoogleKeyBridgeRemains).
'
' WHAT GUARDS IT. internal/contract/model_bridging_retired_test.go, 10 tests:
' no bridge table · no entrypoint bridges a model by role · one Google-key
' alias · no entrypoint reads a role name, and that guard demonstrably fires ·
' no opencode seed names a model by environment · --local-model still selects
' one for opencode · every harness names its local model without a role name ·
' CODING_HARNESSES.md asks for no role bridging · the def image suites assert
' the retirement. The guards read CODE, not comments: this repo names deleted
' machinery where it used to live, and a guard that forbids the explanation
' gets deleted. The image half needs a built image, so `go test ./...` never
' sees it: internal/imagetest/{opencode,cursor,codex}_test.go assert a role
' name reaches the harness as nothing and the harness's OWN var survives; the
' detached smoke's .env carries only each harness's own model vars.
' The role-name guard matches on a WORD BOUNDARY. An agent's own variables are
' named after the same roles (OPENCODE_SMALL_MODEL, ANTHROPIC_SMALL_FAST_MODEL), and
' those must remain; a substring test would flag every one and be deleted.
' The seed guard exists because the retirement itself SHIPPED that defect: the
' run after the deletion wrote model="" into the durable home, where it
' outlives the session — the opposite of "the agent's own default applies".
' It is a Go test beside its image twin (internal/imagetest/opencode_test.go),
' because the image suite needs a built image and this must fail in
' `go test ./...`.
' Two image suites once asserted the BRIDGE — ARCHITECT_MODEL became
' OPENCODE_MODEL, then CURSOR_MODEL — and, needing a built image, neither
' failed in `go test ./...`; they would have failed after the deletion merged.
' So the Go guard names the REPLACEMENT assertions instead of banning role
' names. A suite proving a name goes nowhere has to say the name, and no regex
' over those files can tell that apart from a suite asserting the bridge.
'
' ── RETIRED 2026-09-09. THE DIAGRAM BELOW DESCRIBES A MECHANISM THAT IS GONE ─
' The TSV tables, apply_model_bridges and the role vars it documents were
' deleted by the decision above.
'
' The file is KEPT rather than deleted because one fact in it outlives the
' mechanism and is written down nowhere else: claudecode's ANTHROPIC_MODEL and
' ANTHROPIC_SMALL_FAST_MODEL take a BARE id, so a provider-qualified name
' reaches the vendor with the one token identifying the vendor stripped off.
' Nothing enforces that today. If a future change ever writes those variables
' again, this is the trap it must not walk into.
'
' UPDATE 2026-10-17 (N1, then N2 + N23 + N22; MEASURED, wt): NOTHING of the
' mechanism below remains on either side. internal/entrypoint holds only
' EnsureRuntimeUser and firstNonEmpty (ApplyEnvBridges, BridgeGoogleKeys,
' NormalizeModel deleted by N1; SmokeReady by N22). The bash remnant —
' _normalize_model, _apply_env_bridge, apply_env_bridges and the uncalled
' _model_provider — is deleted too (N2 + N23), with the opencode and hermes
' calls to apply_env_bridges; the five-line bridge_google_keys
' (entrypoint-lib.sh:36-40) is the one alias left, and
' TestOneGoogleKeyBridgeRemains (model_bridging_retired_test.go:65) pins it and
' bans the four names. The prefix table, "Go/bash parity" and "two consumers"
' text below therefore describe code that no longer exists on EITHER side.
'
' ── VENDOR-LOCKED SLOTS: WHY A FILTER, AND WHY DECLARED ────────────────────
' A slot may name the only provider it accepts (column 6 of the TSV). Today that
' is claudecode's two: ANTHROPIC_MODEL and ANTHROPIC_SMALL_FAST_MODEL.
'
' The transform is what makes it necessary rather than tidy. Those rows carry
' ""bare"", which STRIPS the provider/ prefix — so ARCHITECT_MODEL=openai/gpt-5
' reaches the agent as ANTHROPIC_MODEL=gpt-5: the one token identifying the
' vendor discarded, and an id api.anthropic.com has never heard of left looking
' plausible. The operator reads a model name in the header, the agent sends it,
' and the 404 names neither the model nor the mistake.
'
' DECLARED, NOT DERIVED. ANTHROPIC_MODEL looks derivable from its own name, but
' OPENCODE_MODEL does not: ""opencode"" is a provider in the registry AND a
' harness, and that slot's default is ""anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-5"" — deriving
' the lock from the variable name would refuse the default it ships with.
'
' UNRESOLVABLE IS ACCEPTED. ModelProvider returns "" for ollama, ollama_chat and
' openai-compatible, because those endpoints serve arbitrary ids. Refusing what
' cannot be classified would break --local-model, which points a role at an
' ollama id on purpose. The shell agreed only after a fix: it resolved
' ollama/llama3 to "ollama" and would have refused it from a locked slot while
' the host header showed it accepted — caught by the parity test, not by review.
'
' THE PROVIDER IS THE RULE, NOT THE FAMILY. opus/sonnet/haiku are what an
' operator names, but the check asks ModelProvider — so claude-fable-5 and any
' future Anthropic family pass without a table edit, and the registry stays the
' one place a model's vendor is decided.
'
' ── HOW A ROW IS APPLIED, AND WHY THE FILE'S ORDER IS PART OF THE DATA ─────
' A TSV row is: slot, targets, roles, default, transform, want. Applied in file
' order, and ROW ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING: a "$VAR" default must run AFTER the row
' that sets VAR. A `$`-prefixed default means "read this other environment
' variable", not "use this literal"; a bare "-" means no default.
'
' Within a row: the first non-empty variable in `roles` wins, then the default;
' `targets` is a comma-separated list and each target is skipped when it is
' ALREADY set, so an explicit tool-specific value always beats the alias.
' Comment rows (#) and empty slots are ignored, so a table can carry its own
' documentation.
'
' The vendor lock is checked BEFORE the transform, since `bare` is what would
' discard the evidence. Transforms are `normalize` (prefix a bare id with its
' provider) and `bare` (strip the provider/ prefix).
'
' ── THE PREFIX TABLE LIVES IN EXACTLY ONE PLACE PER SIDE ───────────────────
' _normalize_model is that place in the shell: gpt-*/chatgpt-* and OpenAI's
' reasoning ids (the letter "o" followed by a digit — o1, o3, o4-mini) go to
' openai/, claude-* to anthropic/, grok-* to xai/, gemini-* to google/,
' deepseek-* to deepseek/. An id that already contains "/" is returned as-is.
'
' _model_provider is built ON TOP of _normalize_model rather than repeating the
' table, and internal/contract runs one table through both it and
' provider.ModelProvider so the two cannot drift.
'
' REFUSAL IS REPORTED. A locked slot that silently stays unset leaves the agent
' on its own built-in default: a working run producing work on a model nobody
' chose, which is the quietest kind of wrong. RefusedSlots names the variable,
' both vendors and the consequence, before launch on the host and again in the
' container.
'
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title Model choice — no model by environment; the retired alias tables, three harness dialects
' purpose: why proveo chooses no agent model by environment, what guards that, and the alias tables it retired
' covers: internal/entrypoint/**
' covers: packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh
' covers: internal/contract/model_bridging_retired_test.go
' covers: CODING_HARNESSES.md
' covers: defs/opencode/sample_opencode.json
' covers: defs/opencode/defaults/opencode.json
' Notes here are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.

folder "Host" as HOST <<host>> {
  component "host env  or  host-side .env\nARCHITECT_MODEL · EDITOR_MODEL · SMALL_MODEL\nDARK_MODE · CODE_THEME" as SRC <<host>>
  component "cmd/proveo run\nforwards entrypoint.ConfigVars by value" as RUN <<app>>
}

node "Agent container" as CTR <<host>> {
  component "docker run -e ARCHITECT_MODEL=…" as ENVIN <<app>>
  component "apply_model_bridges <harness>\ndefs/bridges/<harness>.tsv" as BRIDGE <<app>>

  component "opencode — models.dev ids,\nprovider-prefixed\nOPENCODE_MODEL · OPENCODE_BUILD_MODEL\nOPENCODE_SMALL_MODEL" as OC <<app>>
  component "claudecode — bare vendor ids\nANTHROPIC_MODEL\nANTHROPIC_SMALL_FAST_MODEL" as CC <<app>>
  component "cursor — bare vendor ids\nCURSOR_MODEL" as CU <<app>>
}

cloud "Ollama sidecar\n--local-model" as OLLAMA <<cloud>>

SRC ARROW_MAIN RUN
RUN ARROW_MAIN ENVIN : " ""-e NAME=value"" "
ENVIN ARROW_MAIN BRIDGE
BRIDGE ARROW_MAIN OC : normalize → ""provider/model""
BRIDGE ARROW_MAIN CC : bare id\n(strip ""provider/"" prefix)
BRIDGE ARROW_MAIN CU : bare id
OLLAMA ARROW_CLOUD ENVIN : overrides all three tiers\n(""-e"" applied after Env)

note top of SRC
  **No two agents spell a model the same way.**
  That is the only reason these aliases exist: an
  operator names a tier once and each harness
  receives the dialect it parses, rather than
  learning three vocabularies to switch tools.
end note

note bottom of SRC
  **Versions are spelled inconsistently too.**
  OpenRouter dots the version where the vendor
  dashes it, Vertex and Bedrock stamp a date, and
  Bedrock prefixes ""anthropic."" — so comparison
  normalizes before it decides anything.
end note

note right of RUN
  **Forwarded by value, never through .env.**
  Brokered tiers mask every dotenv file under the
  mounted tree and the ""app"" layout never mounts
  one, so the documented alias contract silently
  did nothing in the default egress mode.
end note

note bottom of RUN
  **Secrets never travel this path.** They are
  declared manifest env, brokered, or withheld,
  because a non-secret ""-e"" pair stays visible
  to anything permitted to inspect the container.
end note

note top of BRIDGE
  **One table, two consumers.** Every mapping is
  declared in ""defs/bridges/<harness>\.tsv"": the
  shell applies it at container start and the host
  reads the same rows, embedded, to show resolved
  slots before a container exists.
end note

note bottom of BRIDGE
  **Every bridge runs in the def's own shell,**
  because ""proveo-entrypoint prep"" cannot export
  into its parent process. That boundary is what
  rules out a single Go implementation, however
  much tidier one would read.
end note

note left of BRIDGE
  **Precedence is the same for every harness.**
  An explicit tool-specific value already set
  always wins, the alias only fills an empty slot,
  and ""--local-model"" beats both because it
  redirects every tier at the sidecar.
end note

note right of BRIDGE
  **Tier mapping is not uniform, on purpose.**
  Opencode prefers ""EDITOR_MODEL"" for its small
  slot while claudecode maps
  ""SMALL_MODEL"" straight through, so the table
  keeps each dialect instead of averaging them.
end note

note bottom of CU
  **Vendor-pinned.** Cursor takes no custom base
  url, so ""--local-model"" is refused rather than
  ignored: an operator expecting a local sidecar
  would otherwise be billed for remote calls.
end note

note top of ENVIN
  **Validation warns and never rejects.** The list
  of known ids lags the vendors, so an unknown
  model is usually newer than the binary rather
  than mistyped, and refusing it would block
  legitimate upgrades.
end note

note bottom of ENVIN
  **This catches one specific failure.** A
  mistyped tier otherwise reaches the container
  and returns 404 on every invocation, with a
  vendor error that reads like an outage rather
  than a simple typo.
end note

@enduml
